`charge under s 506` with `Chan Yok Tuang, the facts as they were` 's `refusal` is equal to A charge under section 506 would assert that the facts fulfil every legal condition of criminal intimidation (CPC s 123(5)). On the facts given they do not: with intent to cause alarm to that person, or to cause that person to do any act which he is not legally bound to do, or to omit to do any act which that person is legally entitled to do; the elements of section 503 taken together.
`commits criminal intimidation` with `Chan Yok Tuang, with intent to alarm`
`charge under s 506` with `Chan Yok Tuang, with intent to alarm` 's `made out`
`charge under s 506` with `Chan Yok Tuang, with intent to alarm` 's `text` is equal to You, Chan Yok Tuang, are charged that you, on or about 16 May 2007, at the Central Police Division lockup, Singapore, did commit criminal intimidation by threatening to cause injury to the person of SSSgt Jessie Lim Geok Hwee; to wit, by uttering “I will shoot her to death” in Hokkien at her, with intent to cause alarm to the said SSSgt Jessie Lim Geok Hwee, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 506 of the Penal Code 1871.
`the threat falls within the aggravated limb of s 506` with `Chan Yok Tuang, with intent to alarm`
`charge under s 506` with `Chan Yok Tuang, with intent to alarm` 's `punishment` is equal to imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, or with fine, or with both
`charge under s 506` with `Chan Yok Tuang, threat not aggravated` 's `made out`
not `the threat falls within the aggravated limb of s 506` with `Chan Yok Tuang, threat not aggravated`
`charge under s 506` with `Chan Yok Tuang, threat not aggravated` 's `punishment` is equal to imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both
`commits criminal intimidation` with `the Illustration to s 503`
`the threat falls within the aggravated limb of s 506` with `the Illustration to s 503`
`charge under s 506` with `the Illustration to s 503` 's `text` is equal to You, A, are charged that you, on or about 1 January 2026, at the dwelling-house of the said B, Singapore, did commit criminal intimidation by threatening to cause injury to the property of B, the plaintiff in the said civil suit, with intent to cause the said B to omit to do an act which he is legally entitled to do, as the means of avoiding the execution of the said threat, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 506 of the Penal Code 1871.
